@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@
+# Custom images, SSBOs and compute programs
+
+This backend implements these resource paths through Metal. It is not a claim of
+complete OpenGL 4.3 conformance.
+
+## Supported paths
+
+- `image2D`, `iimage2D`, `uimage2D`, `image3D`, `iimage3D`, and `uimage3D`,
+  including arrays of image uniforms, in vertex, fragment and compute programs.
+  Image uniforms participate in active-uniform queries and `glUniform1i/1iv`.
+  GLSL constant expressions and macros in `layout(binding=...)` are preserved.
+- `glBindImageTexture` resolves the current texture allocation when drawing or
+  dispatching. A binding may precede allocation. A nonzero mip selects a
+  single-level Metal view, so shader image coordinates and `imageSize` refer to
+  that mip. Use `layered=GL_TRUE` for `image3D`.
+- Signed/unsigned R, RG and RGBA integer textures with 8-, 16- and 32-bit
+  components. Uploads, clears and readback preserve all 32 bits, support integer
+  width conversion and use `GL_*_INTEGER` external formats. Pixel-store row/image
+  strides, skips, alignment and byte swapping apply to transfers.
+- `glTexStorage2D` for 2D/cube textures and `glTexStorage3D` for 3D textures,
+  with immutable format/level queries. `glTexSubImage*` can populate the storage;
+  `glTexImage*` cannot redefine it. Mutable texture allocation remains available.
+- SSBOs in graphics and compute programs: `std430`/`std140` layouts, scalar,
+  vector and matrix members, nested structures/arrays, runtime tails,
+  read/write access and atomics. Program-resource queries expose leaf member
+  offsets, matrix/array strides and top-level array metadata. Anonymous block
+  members omit the block-name prefix.
+- `glBindBufferBase`, `glBindBufferRange`, `glShaderStorageBlockBinding` and
+  runtime-array `.length()` using the bound range. `GL_BUFFER_DATA_SIZE` includes
+  one runtime-tail element; range validation allows a zero-element tail.
+- Buffer allocation, subdata, copy, clear, readback and nonpersistent mapping.
+  Partial CPU updates wait for preceding GPU uses so untouched SSBO bytes retain
+  GPU writes. Whole-store replacement can rename the allocation. Mapping queries
+  report the actual range, flags and pointer; `glBufferData` implicitly unmaps.
+- Compute compilation diagnostics, link-time local-size validation, 3D dispatch,
+  shared memory, barriers, `gl_NumWorkGroups`, and GPU-generated indirect dispatch
+  arguments. Compute and render encoders are ordered through the same command
+  queue. `glMemoryBarrier` ends the active encoder to establish visibility for
+  subsequent commands; synchronized CPU access also waits for completion.
+
+Example of a 3D compute image and ranged SSBO:
+
+```glsl
+#version 430
+layout(local_size_x=4, local_size_y=4, local_size_z=4) in;
+layout(r32ui, binding=0) uniform uimage3D volume;
+layout(std430, binding=1) buffer Output { uint values[]; } outputData;
+
+void main() {
+    ivec3 p = ivec3(gl_GlobalInvocationID);
+    if (any(greaterThanEqual(p, imageSize(volume)))) return;
+    uint value = imageLoad(volume, p).x + 1u;
+    imageStore(volume, p, uvec4(value));
+    ivec3 size = imageSize(volume);
+    uint index = uint(p.x + size.x * (p.y + size.y * p.z));
+    if (index < uint(outputData.values.length())) outputData.values[index] = value;
+}
+```
+
+```cpp
+glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_3D, texture);
+glTexStorage3D(GL_TEXTURE_3D, 1, GL_R32UI, width, height, depth);
+glClearTexImage(texture, 0, GL_RED_INTEGER, GL_UNSIGNED_INT, nullptr);
+glBindImageTexture(0, texture, 0, GL_TRUE, 0, GL_READ_WRITE, GL_R32UI);
+glBindBufferRange(GL_SHADER_STORAGE_BUFFER, 1, buffer, offset, size);
+glUseProgram(computeProgram);
+glDispatchCompute((width + 3) / 4, (height + 3) / 4, (depth + 3) / 4);
+glMemoryBarrier(GL_SHADER_IMAGE_ACCESS_BARRIER_BIT | GL_SHADER_STORAGE_BARRIER_BIT);
+```
+
+## Device requirements and limits
+
+The existing compute capability gate requires Apple GPU family 6 or newer, at
+least 32 KiB threadgroup memory, and the exposed workgroup limits. Query the
+`GL_MAX_COMPUTE_*`, SSBO and image limits rather than assuming desktop limits.
+Vertex/fragment images share each stage's 32 Metal texture slots with samplers.
+
+Native image atomics require iOS 17+, Apple GPU family 6+, and R32I/R32UI storage.
+These devices use MSL 3.1. Older supported configurations use MSL 2.2, and
+programs needing an auxiliary buffer for emulated image atomics fail linking
+with an explanation. SSBO/shared-memory atomics do not require texture atomics.
+
+Remaining limitations:
+
+- Storage images are non-multisampled 2D or layered 3D. Array/cube/buffer images
+  and an individual 3D slice bound as `image2D` are not implemented.
+- Image views use `GL_IMAGE_FORMAT_COMPATIBILITY_BY_CLASS`, and Metal must also
+  accept the requested pixel-format view. Image signedness, access mode, declared
+  format, dimensions and mip are validated before encoding a draw/dispatch.
+  Use matching R32I/R32UI storage for image atomics.
+- Persistent/coherent buffer mappings, arrays of SSBO blocks, atomic-counter
+  buffers and separate program pipelines are outside this implementation.
+- Existing packed-color texture upload restrictions remain. The integer transfer
+  path described above uses scalar byte/short/int types, not packed integer types.
+- CPU tests and native compilation cannot establish Metal execution correctness;
+  run the device test below before relying on a particular iOS/GPU combination.
+
+## Tests
+
+Initialize the pinned submodules, then run the portable tests on Windows, macOS
+or Linux with a C++17 compiler and CMake 3.22.1 or newer:
+
+```sh
+git submodule update --init --recursive
+cmake -S . -B build/tests -DGL4METAL_TRANSLATOR_TESTS_ONLY=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build build/tests --config Release --target translator_tests --parallel
+ctest --test-dir build/tests -C Release --output-on-failure
+```
+
+The tests run glslang and SPIRV-Cross, checking image types/bindings, per-stage
+slots, nested SSBO reflection, runtime lengths, workgroup built-ins and native
+atomics. Passing an output directory to `translator_tests` writes MSL fixtures.
+CI compiles those fixtures with Apple's Metal compiler and builds the iOS library
+with the optional device test enabled.
+
+To test on a device, add `-DGL4METAL_GPU_TESTS=ON` to the normal iOS build, load the
+library, and call the exported function on the GL submission thread in a fresh
+context before application rendering:
+
+```cpp
+extern "C" int gl4metalRunResourceTests();
+int result = gl4metalRunResourceTests(); // 0: passed, 1: failed, 77: unsupported
+```
+
+This opt-in test changes GL bindings and deletes its own objects. It verifies
+immutable 3D mips, exact integer upload/readback, ranged SSBO writes and clears,
+preservation of GPU writes during a partial CPU update, GPU-generated indirect
+dispatch, mapped-range queries/errors, and image/SSBO/shared-memory atomics on
+iOS 17+. Failures are reported through `GL4METAL_LOG`.
